:: dialog/maren/backstory-1 [dialog maren]
Maren — Local Shopkeeper
"The community room. That's where I kept
the last of the supplies. I know what's left."

:: dialog/maren/backstory-2 [dialog maren]
"I've been walking the same block
for... I don't know how long. Thank you."

"Take what you need from what I have."

:: dialog/maren/backstory-3 [dialog maren]
"I'll help you map what's still usable
in here. There's more to this city
than anyone told us."

[Maren joins your cause. They are waiting for you at the Community Room.]

:: dialog/maren/to-player-first [dialog maren]
"You're the one who found me walking.
I don't know how to thank someone for that."
---
"...you just did."

Saying it out loud feels like unsealing a door.

:: dialog/maren/waiting [dialog maren]
"When you need the shelves counted,
you know where I am. Careful out there."
